IMPORT prelude

-- Three-valued helpers used by the rule modules.
-- A result is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE, or NOTHING (the text does not say).
-- They carry no provision of their own, so they carry no @ref.

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`both results hold` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (a EQUALS JUST FALSE) OR (b EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (a EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (b EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`either result holds` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (a EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (b EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST TRUE
           IF (a EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (b EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the opposite of a result` MEANS
    BRANCH IF a EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
           IF a EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN results IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`every result in a list holds` MEANS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, x YIELD `both results hold` acc x) (JUST TRUE) results

GIVEN results IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`some result in a list holds` MEANS
    foldl (GIVEN acc, x YIELD `either result holds` acc x) (JUST FALSE) results
